.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_GENERATE_NCONF 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_generate_nconf ,
.Nm ASN1_generate_v3
.Nd ASN1 string generation functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft ASN1_TYPE *
.Fo ASN1_generate_nconf
.Fa "const char *str"
.Fa "CONF *nconf"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_TYPE *
.Fo ASN1_generate_v3
.Fa "const char *str"
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *cnf"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions generate the ASN1 encoding of a string in an
.Vt ASN1_TYPE
structure.
.Pp
.Fa str
contains the string to encode.
.Fa nconf
or
.Fa cnf
contains the optional configuration information where additional strings
will be read from.
.Fa nconf
will typically come from a config file whereas
.Fa cnf
is obtained from an
.Vt X509V3_CTX
structure, which will typically be used by X509 v3 certificate extension
functions.
.Fa cnf
or
.Fa nconf
can be set to NULL if no additional configuration will be used.
.Sh GENERATION STRING FORMAT
The actual data encoded is determined by the string
.Fa str
and the configuration information.
The general format of the string is:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It [ Ns Em modifier Ns ,] Ns Em type Ns [: Ns Em value ]
.El
That is zero or more comma separated modifiers followed by a type
followed by an optional colon and a value.
The formats of
.Em type ,
.Em value
and
.Em modifier
are explained below.
.Ss Supported Types
The supported types are listed below.
Case is not significant in the type names.
Unless otherwise specified only the
.Sy ASCII
format is permissible.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy BOOLEAN Ns , Sy BOOL
This encodes a boolean type.
The
.Em value
string is mandatory and should be
.Sy TRUE
or
.Sy FALSE .
Additionally
.Sy TRUE ,
.Sy true ,
.Sy Y ,
.Sy y ,
.Sy YES ,
.Sy yes ,
.Sy FALSE ,
.Sy false ,
.Sy N ,
.Sy n ,
.Sy NO
and
.Sy no
are acceptable.
.It Dv NULL
Encode the
.Dv NULL
type, the
.Em value
string must not be present.
.It Sy INTEGER Ns , Sy INT
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy INTEGER
type.
The
.Em value
string represents the value of the integer, it can be prefaced by a
minus sign and is normally interpreted as a decimal value unless the
prefix
.Sy 0x
is included.
.It Sy ENUMERATED Ns , Sy ENUM
Encodes the ASN1
.Sy ENUMERATED
type, it is otherwise identical to
.Sy INTEGER .
.It Sy OBJECT Ns , Sy OID
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy OBJECT IDENTIFIER ,
the
.Em value
string can be a short name, a long name or numerical format.
.It Sy UTCTIME Ns , Sy UTC
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy UTCTime
structure, the value should be in the format
.Sy YYMMDDHHMMSSZ .
.It Sy GENERALIZEDTIME Ns , Sy GENTIME
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy GeneralizedTime
structure, the value should be in the format
.Sy YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ .
.It Sy OCTETSTRING Ns , Sy OCT
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy OCTET STRING .
.Em value
represents the contents of this structure, the format strings
.Sy ASCII
and
.Sy HEX
can be used to specify the format of
.Em value .
.It Sy BITSTRING Ns , Sy BITSTR
Encodes an ASN1
.Sy BIT STRING .
.Em value
represents the contents of this structure, the format strings
.Sy ASCII ,
.Sy HEX
and
.Sy BITLIST
can be used to specify the format of
.Em value .
.Pp
If the format is anything other than
.Sy BITLIST
the number of unused bits is set to zero.
.It Sy UNIVERSALSTRING Ns , Sy UNIV Ns , Sy IA5 Ns , Sy IA5STRING Ns , Sy UTF8 Ns , Sy UTF8String Ns , Sy BMP Ns , Sy BMPSTRING Ns , Sy VISIBLESTRING Ns , Sy VISIBLE Ns , Sy PRINTABLESTRING Ns , Sy PRINTABLE Ns , Sy T61 Ns , Sy T61STRING Ns , Sy TELETEXSTRING Ns , Sy GeneralString Ns , Sy NUMERICSTRING Ns , Sy NUMERIC
These encode the corresponding string types.
.Em value
represents the contents of this structure.
The format can be
.Sy ASCII
or
.Sy UTF8 .
.It Sy SEQUENCE Ns , Sy SEQ Ns , Sy SET
Formats the result as an ASN1
.Sy SEQUENCE
or
.Sy SET
type.
.Em value
should be a section name which will contain the contents.
The field names in the section are ignored and the values are in the
generated string format.
If
.Em value
is absent then an empty SEQUENCE will be encoded.
.El
.Ss Modifiers
Modifiers affect the following structure, they can be used to add
EXPLICIT or IMPLICIT tagging, add wrappers or to change the string
format of the final type and value.
The supported formats are documented below.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy EXPLICIT Ns , Sy EXP
Add an explicit tag to the following structure.
This string should be followed by a colon and the tag value to use as a
decimal value.
.Pp
By following the number with
.Sy U ,
.Sy A ,
.Sy P
or
.Sy C
UNIVERSAL, APPLICATION, PRIVATE or CONTEXT SPECIFIC tagging can be used,
the default is CONTEXT SPECIFIC.
.It Sy IMPLICIT Ns , Sy IMP
This is the same as
.Sy EXPLICIT
except IMPLICIT tagging is used instead.
.It Sy OCTWRAP Ns , Sy SEQWRAP Ns , Sy SETWRAP Ns , Sy BITWRAP
The following structure is surrounded by an OCTET STRING, a SEQUENCE, a
SET or a BIT STRING respectively.
For a BIT STRING the number of unused bits is set to zero.
.It Sy FORMAT
This specifies the format of the ultimate value.
It should be followed by a colon and one of the strings
.Sy ASCII ,
.Sy UTF8 ,
.Sy HEX
or
.Sy BITLIST .
.Pp
If no format specifier is included then
.Sy ASCII
is used.
If
.Sy UTF8
is specified then the value string must be a valid
.Sy UTF8
string.
For
.Sy HEX
the output must be a set of hex digits.
.Sy BITLIST
(which is only valid for a BIT STRING) is a comma separated list of the
indices of the set bits, all other bits are zero.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ASN1_generate_nconf
and
.Fn ASN1_generate_v3
return the encoded data as an
.Vt ASN1_TYPE
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Pp
The error codes that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
A simple IA5String:
.Bd -literal
 IA5STRING:Hello World
.Ed
.Pp
An IA5String explicitly tagged:
.Bd -literal
 EXPLICIT:0,IA5STRING:Hello World
.Ed
.Pp
An IA5String explicitly tagged using APPLICATION tagging:
.Bd -literal
 EXPLICIT:0A,IA5STRING:Hello World
.Ed
.Pp
A BITSTRING with bits 1 and 5 set and all others zero:
.Bd -literal
 FORMAT:BITLIST,BITSTRING:1,5
.Ed
.Pp
A more complex example using a config file to produce a SEQUENCE
consisting of a BOOL an OID and a UTF8String:
.Bd -literal
 asn1 = SEQUENCE:seq_section

 [seq_section]

 field1 = BOOLEAN:TRUE
 field2 = OID:commonName
 field3 = UTF8:Third field
.Ed
.Pp
This example produces an RSAPrivateKey structure, this is the key
contained in the file client.pem in all OpenSSL distributions (note: the
field names such as 'coeff' are ignored and are present just for
clarity):
.Bd -literal
 asn1=SEQUENCE:private_key
 [private_key]
 version=INTEGER:0

 n=INTEGER:0xBB6FE79432CC6EA2D8F970675A5A87BFBE1AFF0BE63E879F2AFFB93644\e
 D4D2C6D000430DEC66ABF47829E74B8C5108623A1C0EE8BE217B3AD8D36D5EB4FCA1D9

 e=INTEGER:0x010001

 d=INTEGER:0x6F05EAD2F27FFAEC84BEC360C4B928FD5F3A9865D0FCAAD291E2A52F4A\e
 F810DC6373278C006A0ABBA27DC8C63BF97F7E666E27C5284D7D3B1FFFE16B7A87B51D

 p=INTEGER:0xF3929B9435608F8A22C208D86795271D54EBDFB09DDEF539AB083DA912\e
 D4BD57

 q=INTEGER:0xC50016F89DFF2561347ED1186A46E150E28BF2D0F539A1594BBD7FE467\e
 46EC4F

 exp1=INTEGER:0x9E7D4326C924AFC1DEA40B45650134966D6F9DFA3A7F9D698CD4ABEA\e
 9C0A39B9

 exp2=INTEGER:0xBA84003BB95355AFB7C50DF140C60513D0BA51D637272E355E397779\e
 E7B2458F

 coeff=INTEGER:0x30B9E4F2AFA5AC679F920FC83F1F2DF1BAF1779CF989447FABC2F5\e
 628657053A
.Ed
.Pp
This example is the corresponding public key in a SubjectPublicKeyInfo
structure:
.Bd -literal
 # Start with a SEQUENCE
 asn1=SEQUENCE:pubkeyinfo

 # pubkeyinfo contains an algorithm identifier and the public key wrapped
 # in a BIT STRING
 [pubkeyinfo]
 algorithm=SEQUENCE:rsa_alg
 pubkey=BITWRAP,SEQUENCE:rsapubkey

 # algorithm ID for RSA is just an OID and a NULL
 [rsa_alg]
 algorithm=OID:rsaEncryption
 parameter=NULL

 # Actual public key: modulus and exponent
 [rsapubkey]
 n=INTEGER:0xBB6FE79432CC6EA2D8F970675A5A87BFBE1AFF0BE63E879F2AFFB93644\e
 D4D2C6D000430DEC66ABF47829E74B8C5108623A1C0EE8BE217B3AD8D36D5EB4FCA1D9

 e=INTEGER:0x010001
.Ed
